# Cavernous Maw counts "the number of Cave cards in your graveyard" with the other Caves you control (CR 602.5b, 205.3i): Thought Scour
# mills two Captivating Caves into Bot1's graveyard, which with no other Cave in play makes two and the {2} ability is refused (two
# Moxen could pay it); playing a Captivating Cave makes one other Cave plus two in the graveyard, three exactly, and the Moxen pay
# exactly its {2}. The Maw is a 3/3 Elemental (and still a Cave land) until end of turn.

